 "result": "fibmod.py computes fib(n) mod 1e9+7 by fast doubling over the bits of n (about 60 steps for n up to 10**18), reading all of stdin and writing one result per line. It matches the public sample out-0.txt byte for byte and gives fib(10)=55 and fib(0)=0. The assay registered a baseline of 2.62672 with 1.5% noise. A variant with fewer modular reductions and a start that skips the leading bit then measured +6% and was adopted. I am resting here because the remaining ideas are likely to gain less than the 3% needed to count as a win.",
